# ── Public site URL (used for canonical URLs, sitemap, OG tags) ──
# No trailing slash. Set to your real domain in production.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://ozzo.co.in

# ── Supabase (wacrm project) — used server-side to store inquiries ──
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://gxurqwpfvfktmreqmzqb.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# ── Email alerts for new inquiries (optional but recommended) ──
# Uses Resend (https://resend.com). Leave RESEND_API_KEY empty to disable
# email — inquiries are still saved to the database.
RESEND_API_KEY=
# Where new-lead alerts are sent (your sales/team inbox):
INQUIRY_NOTIFY_EMAIL=hello@ozzo.co.in
# Verified "from" address on your Resend domain:
INQUIRY_FROM_EMAIL=OZZO Website <notifications@ozzo.co.in>

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Instant lead alerts (optional)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# When a visitor submits the inquiry form, the lead is ALWAYS saved to
# Supabase and emailed via Resend. These variables add instant push
# notifications on top, so nobody has to be watching an inbox.
#
# EVERY channel configured below fires, in parallel. Setting up a second
# one does not switch the first one off.
#
# Leave them all unset and nothing breaks — alerts are skipped exactly
# the way the Resend alert is skipped without a key, and a failing
# channel can never fail a form submission.

# --- Telegram (recommended: free, instant, no extra phone number) ------
# Setup, entirely in the Telegram app, about two minutes:
#   1. Message @BotFather, send /newbot, follow the prompts.
#      It replies with the bot token -> TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN.
#   2. Open your new bot and press START. A bot cannot message anyone
#      who has not started a chat with it first — skipping this gives
#      "chat not found" later, which looks like a bad token but is not.
#   3. Message @userinfobot. It replies with your numeric id
#      -> TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID.
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# --- Generic webhook (any BSP, automation tool, or OZZO's own CRM) -----
# Receives POST {to, text, lead} as JSON.
# WHATSAPP_ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL=
# WHATSAPP_ALERT_WEBHOOK_SECRET=   # optional; sent as "Authorization: Bearer ..."

# --- WhatsApp via Meta Cloud API ---------------------------------------
# NOTE: the SENDER must be a number registered to the Cloud API, and such
# a number can no longer be used in consumer WhatsApp. So it has to be a
# DIFFERENT number from the one printed on the site — which is the
# RECIPIENT below and stays on a normal phone. This is why Telegram is
# the recommended channel: it needs no second number at all.
# WHATSAPP_ALERT_TOKEN=            # permanent System User access token
# WHATSAPP_ALERT_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=  # the sender's Phone Number ID from Meta
#
# Digits only, country code first, no + or spaces. Used by the webhook and
# Cloud API channels. Defaults to contact.whatsappNumber in src/lib/site.ts.
# WHATSAPP_ALERT_TO=919227126301
#
# Cloud API only. A business-initiated message needs an APPROVED template;
# without one WhatsApp only delivers inside a 24h window the recipient
# opened, so set this before relying on it. Category: UTILITY.
# Body must contain exactly six placeholders, in this order:
#   {{1}} name  {{2}} phone  {{3}} company  {{4}} team size  {{5}} page  {{6}} message
# WHATSAPP_ALERT_TEMPLATE=website_lead_alert
# WHATSAPP_ALERT_TEMPLATE_LANG=en
